<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I981ed7d25457381688915171c04a249457a219b5" commit="67dd6f057c707fdfa301a8229c65b256990e2a34" commit_message="scripts: add virtualenv_wrapper  BUG=chromium:645611 TEST=~/chromiumos/chromite/bin$ ./venv_check -&gt; succeeds and prints the correct import path. Also succeeds when run from other cwds.  Change-Id: I981ed7d25457381688915171c04a249457a219b5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388773 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388773" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/73/388773/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4cdd8a5d3bb7f5fb7c76df1801a0d4cc4e8cb679" commit="e229550ff07d2d3542037a15e6e1a8f9ffedca23" commit_message="export_to_gcloud: initial prototype  {&quot;id&quot;: [&quot;Foo&quot;, 1], &quot;foo&quot;: &quot;bar&quot;} {&quot;id&quot;: [&quot;Bar&quot;, 2], &quot;bar&quot;: &quot;baz&quot;} {&quot;id&quot;: [&quot;Bar&quot;, 3], &quot;foo&quot;: &quot;qux&quot;, &quot;parent&quot;: [&quot;Bar&quot;, 2]}  BUG=chromium:645611 TEST=Manual test against test database.  Change-Id: I4cdd8a5d3bb7f5fb7c76df1801a0d4cc4e8cb679 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388916 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388916" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/16/388916/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If41adfd2cba36da7a14c2254fc5df8ec636e3f11" commit="ab6b8ce7c36282a02f7e795747747327975762e0" commit_message="CRAS: alsa_io - Move supported format check  The supported format check will need to be able to access UCM soon. Move it to after ucm is configured so that will be possible.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57838 TEST=alsa_io_unittest  Change-Id: If41adfd2cba36da7a14c2254fc5df8ec636e3f11 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389753 Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="389753" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/53/389753/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8ab41eb4ad015d5b1163a16b617eacdeb31fe20e" commit="430b3c34571c66cc8024082a76518e6ea8f1713f" commit_message="CRAS: alsa_io - Check for set sample rate in UCM  If the UCM config specifies a sample rate, honor it. This is useful for devices where the sample rate must be limited beyond the limits from the driver.  For example there can be valid rates for capture that make playback impossible.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57838 TEST=capture at 44100 and play at 48k on Kevin  Change-Id: I8ab41eb4ad015d5b1163a16b617eacdeb31fe20e Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389754 Reviewed-by: Chinyue Chen &lt;chinyue@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="389754" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/54/389754/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6b0716828d0b360fd6a69348cba432c82b043986" commit="247cd0c66b9ed15e7c0099d20544a609503aa8c7" commit_message="moblab: Fix typo in code  Fix spelling mistake  BUG=chromium:631233 TEST=local  Change-Id: I6b0716828d0b360fd6a69348cba432c82b043986 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390393 Commit-Ready: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="390393" owner_email="haddowk@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/93/390393/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I922710079ac5f4c9ca9c177eab880a99ada1415e" commit="0ceb75bc187d9fe9ec9d3f60f7a22881b1e879be" commit_message="syslinux: drop local copy  We have a newer version in portage-stable now we want to use.  Keep in mind that syslinux is not used on any official Chrome OS device as we have our own custom firmware everywhere.  It is only used when booting Chromium OS.  Our copy had a few custom changes: - Turn off the video cursor before booting the kernel - Sometimes disable display of the syslinux banner when booting - Disable display of all info messages  The first patch is no longer needed: our boot splash code takes care of turning off the cursor before showing the screen, either directly (when USE=vtconsole), or by letting frecon do it when it creates the new VT.  Disabling the boot banner happens only for some boot paths (e.g. the isolinux code), but not all (e.g. the serial port), and it disables only part of the banner.  It also doesn't disable all messages that come up early on.  In the end, it doesn't make things all the much more quiet to the point where we need to maintain it.  The code also tried to disable the common writemsg function, but it is only called for info/debug messages, none of which are displayed by default.  Which means it's kind of a pointless change.  By dropping our custom syslinux version, we make the output a little bit more verbose for Chromium OS builds, but since we aren't silent now, it's not a big deal.  BUG=chromium:508713 TEST=`emerge syslinux` uses the new one in portage-stable TEST=vmtests pass CQ-DEPEND=CL:382771  Change-Id: I922710079ac5f4c9ca9c177eab880a99ada1415e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/382772 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="382772" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/72/382772/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3bc6c3390c6bc631ff78b5747c374a788dfdac60" commit="e2e214b6acf2de4386a7456b1540652a09394266" commit_message="Upload a tarball containing only debug/breakpad.  The new tarball debug_breakpad.tar.xz contains only files in debug/breakpad, which can be used to symbolicate dumps collected during test.  BUG=chromium:623739 TEST=unittest(cbuildbot/run_tests), trybot  Change-Id: I3bc6c3390c6bc631ff78b5747c374a788dfdac60 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388798 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="6" gerrit_number="388798" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/98/388798/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="6"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibd7e120229b0a64b3d38a7cb779d5efbdd8914bd" commit="c121d93de4c4cd9e21f96fbb72b413c18399fdec" commit_message="cros_vm: use the SDK's version of qemu  By default, use the version of qemu shipped with the SDK rather than the default one shipped with the system that may not support all required features (e.g. support for virtio_gpu). This also gives us a more consistent behaviour when VMs are deployed on different hosts with different versions of qemu. Requires CL:351861 so qemu can be used from outside the chroot.  BUG=chromium:618431 BUG=chromium:636309 TEST=cbuildbot --remote cyan-android-pfq after applying CL:389132 to enable VM tests. TEST=cros_run_vm_update --qemu_binary='xxxx' and check that the correct qemu binary gets picked. CQ-DEPEND=CL:351861  Change-Id: Ibd7e120229b0a64b3d38a7cb779d5efbdd8914bd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/389152 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="389152" owner_email="norvez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/52/389152/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I17841a5c5c4aa6a8febc13de482cb0527752ea05" commit="913195be70710a3345ff764320e51fa9854c2bc1" commit_message="Funhaus: Add additional config files  Bug: 31776604 Change-Id: I17841a5c5c4aa6a8febc13de482cb0527752ea05 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390332 Commit-Ready: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Tom Turney &lt;tturney@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390332" owner_email="tturney@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest"